  "query_preview": "..\nAs of 525 AM EST Saturday...\n\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Dry with decreasing winds over the weekend. A \ncold front brings rain and gusty winds Sunday night into Monday. \n\nEarly morning sfc analysis shows low pressure well to the northeast \nand strong high pressure over the gulf. Breezy conditions continue, \nthough winds are ever so slowly diminishing. Latest obs show \nscattered gusts around 20-25mph. High pressure will slide east over \nFL and build northward today, allowing winds to subside this \nevening. Highs will be in upper 50s to around 60. Highs tomorrow \nwill be in the low 60s and cloud cover will increase again ahead of \na cold front. \n\nThe cold front in question is expected to pass through the area \nSunday night into Mon, bringing a round of showers with it. While \nrain rates could be moderate at times (especially north), \noverall precip amounts still look to be fairly low. Ensemble \nprobs for 0.5\" have generally trended upward with 50-70% across\nnorthern portions of the area. However, probs drop off steeply \nafter that and are practically non- existent for 1\". Rain should\nslide offshore by early Monday morning. Sunday night and Monday\nmorning will be breezy again with gusts upwards of 30mph \npossible. A brief cool down with high back to the 50s and lows \ndipping below freezing is expected behind the front Monday \nthrough Wednesday, but this likely won't last long given the \nweak upper level flow depicted in guidance.\n\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...Localized minor coastal flooding continues across\ninterior portions of Virginia Beach early today.\n\nTidal anomalies have dropped significantly over the past 24 \nhours due to the WSW winds. As such, widespread tidal flooding \nis no longer expected, outside of a few stages reaching nuisance\nflood stage. However, the one exception is interior portions of\nVirginia Beach along the North Landing River, West Neck Creek,\nand Back Bay where several gauges have reached minor flood \nstage. Therefore, a Coastal Flood Advisory for Virginia Beach \nhas been extended through 1 PM this afternoon. However, given \nthat the gauges reporting flooding are not tidal and don't have\nmodel data unavailable for them, it is unclear how long these \nsites will remain in minor flood stage. For now, have extended\nthe Coastal Flood Advisory through 1 PM.",
